Upon observing the sequence $\{{\mathssf{g}}_i\}_{i\ge 0}$, the decoder is required to reconstruct each source sequence with zero delay i.e., 
\begin{align}
\hat{{\mathssf{s}}}^{n}_i=\mathcal{G}_{i}({\mathssf{g}}_0, {\mathssf{g}}_1, \ldots, {\mathssf{g}}_{i}, {\mathssf{s}}_{-1}^n), \quad i \notin \{j, \ldots, j+B'+W-1\} \label{eq:decoder-def}
\end{align}
where $\hat{{\mathssf{s}}}_i^{n}$ denotes the reconstruction sequence and $j$ denotes the time at which burst erasure starts in~\eqref{eq:chModel}.

