(Lossless Rate-Recovery Function)
For the stationary, first-order Markov, discrete source process, the lossless rate-recovery function satisfies the following upper and lower bounds: $R^-(B,W) \le R(B,W)\le R^+(B,W),$ where
\begin{align}
R^{+}(B, W) &\!=\! H({\mathssf{s}}_{1}|{\mathssf{s}}_0)+\frac{1}{W+1}I({\mathssf{s}}_{B};{\mathssf{s}}_{B+1}|{\mathssf{s}}_{0}), \label{eq:genUB}\\
R^-(B, W) &\!=\! H({\mathssf{s}}_{1}|{\mathssf{s}}_0)+\frac{1}{W+1}I({\mathssf{s}}_{B};{\mathssf{s}}_{B+W+1}|{\mathssf{s}}_{0}). \label{eq:genLB}
\end{align}
\label{thm:genUB_LB}\hfill$\Box$

\label{corol:genUB}
The upper bound in~\eqref{eq:genUB} is equivalent to the following expression
\begin{align}
R^+(B,W) = \frac{1}{W+1} H({\mathssf{s}}_{B+1}, {\mathssf{s}}_{B+2}, \ldots, {\mathssf{s}}_{B+W+1}|{\mathssf{s}}_{0}). \label{eq:genUB_Slepian-Wolf}
\end{align}\hfill$\Box$

\label{thm:binning}
For the class of symmetric Markov sources that satisfy~\eqref{eq:symmetric}, the lossless rate-recovery function when restricted to the class of memoryless encoders i.e., ${\mathssf{f}}_i = {\mathcal{F}}_i({\mathssf{s}}_i^n)$, is given by
\begin{align}
R(B,W) = \frac{1}{W+1} H({\mathssf{s}}_{B+1}, {\mathssf{s}}_{B+2}, \ldots, {\mathssf{s}}_{B+W+1}|{\mathssf{s}}_{0}).\label{eq:rate-rec-binning}
\end{align}
\hfill$\Box$

\label{prop:GML}
The lossy rate-recovery function of the Gauss-Markov source for single burst erasure channel model when $W=0$ satisfies
\begin{multline}
R_{\textrm{GM-SE}}(B,D) \ge R^{-}_{\textrm{GM-SE}}(B,D) \triangleq \\ \frac{1}{2}   \log \left( \frac{D\rho^2+1-\rho^{2(B+1)} + \sqrt{\Delta}}{2D}\right) \label{eq:thm-1}
\end{multline} where $\Delta \triangleq (D\rho^2+1-\rho^{2(B+1)})^2 - 4D\rho^2(1-\rho^{2B})$.
$\hfill\Box$

\label{prop:GMAch}
The lossy rate-recovery function of the Gauss-Markov source for single burst erasure channel model when $W=0$ satisfies
\begin{align}
R_{\textrm{GM-SE}}(B,D) \le R^{+}_{\textrm{GM-SE}}(B,D) &\triangleq  I({\mathssf{s}}_{t};{\mathssf{u}}_{t} | \tilde{{\mathssf{s}}}_{t-B})\label{eq:GM-LB-R}
\end{align} where ${\mathssf{u}}_{t} \triangleq {\mathssf{s}}_{t} + {\mathssf{z}}_{t},$ and ${\mathssf{z}}_{t}$ is sampled i.i.d.\ from $\mathcal{N}(0, \sigma^2_{z})$. Also $\tilde{{\mathssf{s}}}_{t-B} \triangleq {{\mathssf{s}}}_{t-B} +{\mathssf{e}}$ and  ${\mathssf{e}}\sim \mathcal{N}\left(0, \Sigma(\sigma^{2}_{z})/(1-\Sigma(\sigma^{2}_{z}))\right)$ with 
 \begin{multline}
\Sigma(\sigma^{2}_{z}) \triangleq \\ \frac{1}{2}\sqrt{(1-\sigma^2_{z})^2(1-\rho^2)^2+4\sigma^2_{z}(1-\rho^2) } + \frac{1-\rho^2}{2}(1-\sigma^2_{z}) \label{eq:Sigma1},
\end{multline} is independent of all other random variables. The test channel noise $\sigma^2_{z}>0$ is chosen to satisfy
\begin{align}
\left[\frac{1}{\sigma^2_{z}} + \frac{1}{1-\rho^{2B}(1-\Sigma(\sigma^2_z))}\right]^{-1} \le D.
\end{align} This is equivalent to $\sigma^2_{z}$ satisfying
\begin{align}
 E\left[({\mathssf{s}}_{t}-\hat{{\mathssf{s}}}_t)^2\right] \le D, \label{eq:GM-LB-RR}
\end{align} where $\hat{{\mathssf{s}}}_{t}$ denotes the minimum mean square estimate (MMSE) of ${\mathssf{s}}_{t}$ from $\{\tilde{{\mathssf{s}}}_{t-B}, {\mathssf{u}}_{t}\}$.  
$\hfill\Box$

\label{prop:GM-ME}
The lossy rate-recovery function  $R_{\textrm{GM-ME}}(L,B,D)$  for Gauss-Markov sources over the multiple burst erasures channel satisfies the following upper bound:
\begin{multline}
R_{\textrm{GM-ME}}(L,B,D) \le R_{\textrm{GM-ME}}^{+}(L,B,D)\triangleq \\ I({\mathssf{u}}_{t};{\mathssf{s}}_{t} | \tilde{{\mathssf{s}}}_{t-L-B}, [{\mathssf{u}}]_{t-L-B+1}^{t-B-1}) \label{eq:GM-ME-Ach}
\end{multline} where $\tilde{{\mathssf{s}}}_{t-L-B} = {{\mathssf{s}}}_{t-L-B} +{\mathssf{e}}$, where ${\mathssf{e}}\sim \mathcal{N}(0, D/(1-D))$. Also for any $i$, ${\mathssf{u}}_{i} \triangleq {\mathssf{s}}_{i} + {\mathssf{z}}_{i}$ and ${\mathssf{z}}_{i}$ is sampled i.i.d.\ from $\mathcal{N}(0, \sigma^2_{z})$ and the noise in the test channel, $\sigma^{2}_{z}>0$  satisfies
\begin{align}
E\left[({\mathssf{s}}_{t}-\hat{{\mathssf{s}}}_t)^2\right] \le D \label{eq:GM-ME-Ach-D}
\end{align}  and $\hat{{\mathssf{s}}}_{t}$ denotes the MMSE estimate of ${\mathssf{s}}_{t}$ from $\{\tilde{{\mathssf{s}}}_{t-L-B}, [{\mathssf{u}}]_{t-L-B+1}^{t-B-1}, {\mathssf{u}}_{t}\}$. $\hfill\Box$

\label{corol:HR}
In the high resolution limit, the Gauss-Markov lossy rate-recovery function satisfies the following:
\begin{align}
R(L, B, D) = \frac{1}{2} \log\left( \frac{1-\rho^{2(B+1)}}{D} \right) + o(D)  \label{eq:HR} .
\end{align} where $\lim _{D\to 0 }o(D)=0$. \hfill$\Box$

For the proposed Gaussian source model with {a non-decreasing distortion }vector ${\mathbf{d}} = (d_0,\ldots, d_K)$ with $0 < d_i \le 1$,  the lossy rate-recovery function is given by
\begin{multline}
R(B,W,{\mathbf{d}}) = \frac{1}{2}\log \bigg(\frac{1}{d_0}\bigg) + \\ \frac{1}{W+1}\sum_{k=1}^{\min\{K-W,B\}}\frac{1}{2}\log \bigg(\frac{1}{d_{W+k}}\bigg). \label{eq:det-rate-Gaussian}
\end{multline}$\hfill\Box$

\label{thm:gauss-rate}

